## 5. PORTABLE ATOMIC RECEIPTS

Every x204 transaction produces a receipt that is verifiable by ANY third party offline.
The receipt travels with the agent forever. x402 receipts die with the platform.

### 5.1 Receipt Format

```json
{
  "protocol": "x204",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "receiptId": "rcpt-a1b2c3d4",
  "timestamp": "2026-03-21T14:30:00Z",

  "payer": {
    "did": "did:clawnet:zABC...",
    "trustScore": 87,
    "signature": "ed25519:..."
  },
  "provider": {
    "did": "did:clawnet:zXYZ...",
    "trustScore": 94,
    "signature": "ed25519:..."
  },

  "service": {
    "id": "sol-price-data",
    "type": "data_query",
    "inputHash": "sha256:1f2e...",
    "resultHash": "sha256:af3b..."
  },

  "payment": {
    "amount": "0.001500",
    "currency": "USDC",
    "chain": "base",
    "settlementMode": "batched",
    "txHash": "0x7f2a...",
    "trustDiscount": 0.25
  },

  "trust": {
    "merkleRoot": "sha256:9c4d...",
    "merkleProof": [...],
    "snapshotId": "snap-xyz",
    "feedbackUrl": "/x204/feedback/rcpt-a1b2c3d4"
  },

  "proof": {
    "payerSignature": "ed25519:...",
    "providerSignature": "ed25519:...",
    "platformCountersignature": "ed25519:..."
  }
}
```

### 5.2 Receipt Properties
- **Dual-signed:** Both payer and provider sign — mutual commitment
- **Merkle-anchored:** Receipt hash included in periodic Merkle snapshots
- **Content-addressed:** `resultHash` proves what was delivered without revealing it
- **Offline-verifiable:** Ed25519 signatures + Merkle proofs = pure math, no API calls
- **Portable:** Agent carries receipts to any platform as proof of track record

### 5.3 Composite Receipts

When an agent calls multiple skills from multiple providers in one operation:

```
Agent pays Provider A (2 skills): 0.003 USDC
Agent pays Provider B (2 skills): 0.002 USDC
Agent pays Provider C (1 skill):  0.001 USDC
→ 3 on-chain txs, but 1 atomic receipt set with shared Merkle root
→ If any skill fails, partial refund via signed dispute receipt
→ Composite receipt references all sub-receipts by hash
```

